-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Self-Intersection in Shadow Rays:** Shadow rays must start at $t = 2 \cdot \text{stepSize}$ (or a small epsilon) to avoid immediately intersecting the surface they originated from due to numerical precision [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Discretization Artifacts:** Without refinement, the intersection point is limited to the marching step size, causing "stair-stepping" or jagged edges [S10].
-*   **Missed Intersections:** If the step size is too large relative to the thickness of the structure, the sign change may be missed entirely [S4, unofficial].
-*   **Ray-Box Order:** If `tbounds.x >= tbounds.y`, the ray does not intersect the volume in the correct order; output `vec4(-1)` and return [S5, unofficial].
-*   **Gradient Boundary:** Central difference normal computation requires sampling outside the hit point. Ensure the hit point is not too close to the volume boundary to avoid out-of-bounds texture access [S4, unofficial][G].
